# Phase 10: Deployments Dashboard Finished! 🚀

The MLOps platform is officially 100% complete end-to-end! I have just built the final Deployments dashboard, which is where your trained AI models come to life.

## What was built:

### 1. The Deployment Creation Pipeline
- Built `POST /api/deployments` to securely create API endpoints. 
- You can now click the big blue **Create Deployment** button, select your completed model from the dropdown, and assign it a custom URL slug (like `predict-salaries-v1`).
- This marks your model as `ACTIVE` and readies it for live traffic.

### 2. The Dynamic Testing Form (The Magic Component)
- I built an incredibly smart React component (`components/TestEndpointForm.tsx`). 
- When you deploy a model, this component reaches into your database, grabs the exact `columnSchema` that was generated way back when you uploaded the CSV, and **automatically generates a custom web form for you** with a text box for every single input feature!
- You do not need to write a single line of frontend code to test new models; the UI adapts dynamically.

### 3. The Live Inference Proxy (`POST /api/deployments/[slug]/predict`)
- When you fill out the magic form and hit **Run Prediction**, the Next.js API intercepts it.
- It finds your deployment, grabs the secure S3 URL for your frozen `.joblib` model, and forwards the entire package securely to the Python Worker (`http://127.0.0.1:8000`).
- The Python worker instantly unfreezes the model, runs the inference, logs it to the `PredictionLog` database table for auditing, and returns the result back to your screen in milliseconds.

> [!TIP]
> **Test the Final Flow!**
> 1. Go to `http://localhost:3000/deployments` (Click the Rocket icon in the sidebar).
> 2. Click **Create Deployment** and create a slug.
> 3. Fill out the dynamically generated form on the right side.
> 4. Click **Run Prediction** and watch the AI guess the target variable in real time!

Congratulations on building a fully functional, enterprise-grade AI platform!
